  "report_sha256": "8349c88556f684eaaed5d0ea296e465cddf85086c2d240d30644ecb2e7436625",
  "scope": "Two independent retained sequences use the unchanged worker. Both complete the focus in one advance with 29 entered and stored states; the second 32-entry allowance is not used. Every intermediate catalog, selection, proof, delta and final global result is replayed without fresh discovery or reference search. Seven previously unfinished states are reentered, charged and stored. The false branch reuses its inherited refutation; the new true chain reaches a one-valid terminal outside Horn, dual-Horn and 2-CNF. The enclosing 39/161/495 focus closes, but coverage remains 66/83. Empty saved-split obligations do not imply complete original coverage: 17 originals remain open; the globally selected next source is case 1120, not the completed report source. The reference archive and global positive certificate are byte-identical to the parent. All 3830 reference nodes are independently verified; all prior payloads and 1321 artifacts across 26 manifests are preserved. This is a discovery/reproducibility experiment, with no new speedup, peak-RAM, persistent-space reduction, holdout, Lean theorem or unrestricted-SAT efficiency claim. Tests and the LaTeX build ran concurrently with the start of independent cold validation, after the timed producer had finished.",
